.idea

# Claude Code, shared vs local.
#
# `.claude/settings.json` (the wrap Stop/SessionStart wiring) and
# `.claude/skills/` are checked in deliberately — a clone or a new worktree
# needs both for the hook to run at all.
#
# What stays out is machine- or session-local:
.claude/settings.local.json
# One file per session, keyed by a session UUID, holding three lines derived
# from git. Meaningless in another checkout, rewritten constantly by concurrent
# sessions, and swept on a timer — a tracked copy would conflict, go stale, and
# hand a new worktree some other session's pinned baseline.
.claude/.wrap-state/
